WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:05.910
So, the Season 5 finale of Game Of Thrones
has been and gone, but it's left a shed-load

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:07.890
of questions in its wake.

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:11.900
I've already talked about what the future
holds for Jon Snow and the Night's Watch.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:15.989
In this video, I'm going to look at where
things are headed for Cersei after her Walk

00:00:15.989 --> 00:00:20.609
Of Atonement, and also how this links up with
the future for Jaime and the Martells storyline

00:00:20.609 --> 00:00:22.420
in Dorne in Season 6.

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:28.269
There's going to be speculation and possible
spoilers for the show and the books in this

00:00:28.269 --> 00:00:29.269
video!

00:00:29.269 --> 00:00:33.300
Just before we start, I've got another great
giveaway from our friends at Ten Stickers

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:38.140
who have some insanely cool Game Of Thrones
products as well as loads of other fab movie

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:40.030
and TV stickers.

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:42.700
Details of the giveaway are in the description
below.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:47.820
All you need to do is be a subscriber and
leave a comment on this video about the Lannisters

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:49.300
or Dorne.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:53.830
Remember the flashback we had at start of
season to the prophecy young Cersei received

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:55.100
from Maggy the Frog?

00:00:55.100 --> 00:01:00.110
Well in the proophecy she was told she would
wed a king and she married Robert Baratheon

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:04.460
And she was also told someone younger &amp; more
beautiful would come along to take everything

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:05.830
she held dear.

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:09.590
Well Margaery Tyrell took both her royal title
&amp; her son.

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:14.490
And, as for her children, she was told that:
"gold will be their crowns.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:16.110
Gold their shrouds."

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:21.570
Joffrey was crowned king &amp; poisoned at the
Purple Wedding in Season 4.

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:26.300
Myrcella was also poisoned in the Season 5
finale after a kiss from Ellaria Sand, who

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:29.460
was avenging the death of her lover Oberyn
Martell.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:34.700
Now, of course, Myrcella hasn't been crowned
queen, but "gold will be their crowns" could

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:38.320
have a figurative meaning and just refer to
her golden hair.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:42.200
When the effects of the poison took hold,
Myrcella was sailing back to King's Landing

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:47.610
and enjoying a tender moment with Jaime Lannister,
the man she said she always knew was her father.

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:52.200
But, of course, this is Game Of Thrones, so
that father-daughter bonding lasted about

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:57.270
10 seconds before blood started trickling
from Myrcella's nose and she died.

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:02.031
In the end, then, Oberyn was wrong when he
told Cersei that "We don't hurt little girls

00:02:02.031 --> 00:02:03.031
in Dorne."

00:02:03.031 --> 00:02:08.110
And Cersei was right when she replied, "Everywhere
in the world they hurt little girls."

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:13.659
Oh, and I'm sure that Cersei won't forget
the fact that Tyrion was behind Myrcella's

00:02:13.659 --> 00:02:18.659
Dornish betrothal, and will likely blame him
for Myrcella's murder, just as she did for

00:02:18.659 --> 00:02:19.659
Joffrey's.

00:02:19.659 --> 00:02:24.590
That, of course, leaves Tommen as the final
Lannister child on the list to die.

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:29.859
And if things continue the way they have,
with one death in season 4, another in season

00:02:29.859 --> 00:02:35.239
5, then Tommen looks scheduled to meet his
poisonous end in season 6!

00:02:35.239 --> 00:02:39.959
Obviously, the Tyrells could be out for revenge,
and we they've got form for poisoning people

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:41.069
like Joffrey.

00:02:41.069 --> 00:02:45.109
So perhaps we could see them teaming up with
Littlefinger again.

00:02:45.109 --> 00:02:48.959
But let's go back for a moment, as I want
to talk about what Myrcella's death means

00:02:48.959 --> 00:02:50.340
for Season 6.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:54.480
Throughout Season 5, Prince Doran has been
very keen on keeping the peace between the

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:57.739
Martells in Dorne and the Lannisters in King's
Landing.

00:02:57.739 --> 00:03:02.540
And each time Ellaria Sand and the Sand Snakes
have tried to hatch a plan to get some revenge

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:06.889
for Oberyn's death, they've been foiled, until
the Season 5 finale.

00:03:06.889 --> 00:03:12.499
Ellaria believes Doran is spineless, but Doran
made Ellaria swear allegiance to him, kissing

00:03:12.499 --> 00:03:15.829
his ring, and told her that he believes in
"second chances.

00:03:15.829 --> 00:03:18.700
I don't believe in third chances."

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:25.300
So, by poisoning Myrcella, Ellaria has gone
completely against Doran and his strict instructions

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:28.129
not to harm Cersei's daughter.

00:03:28.129 --> 00:03:32.949
And if Doran finds she'd resposible for Myrcella's
death, she'll doubtless be punished.

00:03:32.949 --> 00:03:37.469
This whole situation will leave Doran's son
Trystane in trouble as he's headed to King's

00:03:37.469 --> 00:03:39.769
Landing on the ship with Jaime, Bronn and
Myrcella.

00:03:39.769 --> 00:03:46.469
Now the Lannisters have a reason for war against
Dorne and a bargaining chip, or rather, a

00:03:46.469 --> 00:03:52.329
means of direct revenge in Trystane, who,
if he ends up in King's Landing, will be in

00:03:52.329 --> 00:03:55.900
a much worse position than Myrcella was in
Dorne.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:04:01.930
After all, Cersei isn't known for being quite
so, err, diplomatic as Prince Doran.

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:07.449
And remember what happened to the last Dornishman
who had a seat on the Small Council?!

00:04:07.449 --> 00:04:12.629
Now, the question is, will Jaime return to
King's Landing or will he turn the ship round

00:04:12.629 --> 00:04:15.530
and head straight back to Dorne to confront
them?

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:20.459
After all, Bronn would likely suspect the
Sand Snakes, given his own experience being

00:04:20.459 --> 00:04:21.459
poisoned!

00:04:21.459 --> 00:04:25.629
I think he'll continue to King's Landing but
I don't think Cersei's going to be too pleased

00:04:25.629 --> 00:04:28.900
when he eventually returns with the news about
Myrcella.

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:33.949
Either way, it's been confirmed that the show
will be filming in Spain again for next season,

00:04:33.949 --> 00:04:36.780
so it's a safe bet we'll see more of Dorne.

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:41.970
Cersei's Walk of Atonement, as the High Sparrow
called it, was more like a Walk of Shame.

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:46.840
That whole sequence was really full-on and
actually made me feel sorry for Cersei.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:52.420
But I'm guessing that won't last next season
as I fully expect her to have learned nothing

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:56.060
from her experiences at the hands of the Faith
Militant.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:58.830
It's unlikely she'll be a reformed character.

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:04.060
She'll probably just have more names on her
hit-list of people to get revenge on in Season

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:05.060
6.

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:10.199
If she wants to stay out of trouble, she better
show a bit more long-term thinking and cunning

00:05:10.199 --> 00:05:12.650
as to how she goes about getting revenge.

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:18.620
I mean, this season, she certainly did nothing
to disprove her father Tywin Lannister's words

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:21.830
that "you're not as smart as you think you
are."

00:05:21.830 --> 00:05:26.780
But she does have her newest King's Guard,
Ser Robert Strong, on her side, who, according

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:33.319
to Qyburn, has taken a vow of silence until
all Cersei's "enemies are dead and the evil

00:05:33.319 --> 00:05:35.909
has been driven from the realm"!

00:05:35.909 --> 00:05:37.409
Sounds ominous!

00:05:37.409 --> 00:05:43.389
In Season 6, Littlefinger, Olenna and Margaery
Tyrell, Septa Unella, Lancel Lannister, the

00:05:43.389 --> 00:05:49.910
High Sparrow, and pretty much anyone and everyone
better watch out, as that guy is a mountain

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:51.110
of a man!

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:56.560
But Cersei had better watch out too if she
tries to take out the High Sparrow as that

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:58.880
could easily cause a rebellion.

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:03.580
Speaking of the High Sparrow, he told Cersei
she'll face a trial to determine whether her

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:06.060
children are bastards, which she denies.

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:10.090
So, who will be lining up to bring evidence?

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:15.060
Given their hardly warm welcome when Cersei
arrived home, Kevan Lannister and Pycelle

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:19.580
seem likely candidates, as does Olenna Tyrell.

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:24.479
Jaime's heading back to King's Landing, so
he could well be called upon to testify too.

00:06:24.479 --> 00:06:30.150
But given Cersei's got this huge new King's
Guard at her disposal, it's much more likely

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:35.110
to end up as a Trial By Combat, like we've
seen previously for Tyrion, once with Bronn

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:37.939
representing him and once with Oberyn stepping
up.

00:06:37.939 --> 00:06:42.349
Wouldn't it be awesome if Cleganebowl actually
happened?!!

00:06:42.349 --> 00:06:46.870
Or could Lancel Lannister step up and fight
for the Faith?

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:53.030
Or total tinfoil hat theory here: what if
Arya took on the face of Sandor Clegane and

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:55.990
fought against the undead Mountain?!!

00:06:55.990 --> 00:07:00.870
Now in the books, there's another line in
Maggy the Frog's prophecy to the young Cersei,

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:03.020
but we haven't heard that the show…

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:04.300
at least not yet.

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:08.860
After Maggy told the young Cersei that her
children would die, she added: "And when your

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:14.830
tears have drowned you, the valonqar shall
wrap his hands about your pale white throat

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:17.370
and choke the life from you."

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:22.319
"Valonqar" means "little brother" in High
Valyrian, and this prophecy has doubtless

00:07:22.319 --> 00:07:25.639
added to Cersei's hatred of Tyrion over the
years.

00:07:25.639 --> 00:07:30.990
So, could this mean that we'll see Tyrion
strangle Cersei, just like he did his former

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:32.039
lover Shae?

00:07:32.039 --> 00:07:35.599
Maggy the Frog's other prophecies have certainly
been coming true.

00:07:35.599 --> 00:07:38.020
I wonder if it'll be that simple though.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:42.139
The mountainous man in armour who scooped
Cersei up into his arms after her walk of

00:07:42.139 --> 00:07:47.440
atonement is Ser Robert Strong, who was created
by Qyburn from the dying Gregor Clegane.

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:53.330
But earlier this season, Qyburn also took
that decapitated dwarf head that looked a

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:56.810
lot like Tyrion to use for his work.

00:07:56.810 --> 00:08:03.120
So, final tinfoil hat theory for this video:
could Qyburn have done a Frankenstein's Monster

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:08.150
and put the Tyrion look-a-like head on top
of the Mountain to make Ser Robert?!

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:14.050
If so, and if Maggy's prophecy comes true,
maybe it's Ser Robert who chokes Cersei…

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:19.009
I mean, the Mountain certainly found it easy
enough to squeeze the life out of Oberyn Martell.

00:08:19.009 --> 00:08:20.199
Something to think about!

00:08:20.199 --> 00:08:25.789
But if Cleganebowl did happen, then of course,
Sandor Clegane is the "little brother" of

00:08:25.789 --> 00:08:35.100
Gregor, so, in that scenario, Sandor could
be the one strangling Cersei!

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:40.590
Now, Qyburn's brought Gregor back from the
dead, maybe he'd like to try doing the same

00:08:40.590 --> 00:08:41.590
for Myrcella?

00:08:41.590 --> 00:08:46.810
But, frankly, I think one zombie in the Lannister
line-up is enough for Season 6!

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:51.350
Going back to the valonqar prophecy, though,
who do you reckon it will turn out to be?

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:55.210
Could it be Cersei's slightly younger twin
brother, Jaime?!

00:08:55.210 --> 00:09:02.590
Then again there’s Tommen, or Trystane Martell,
who’s the youngest son in the books.

00:09:02.590 --> 00:09:07.190
Or perhaps Littlefinger, who Catelyn Stark
viewed as a kind of brother?!

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:11.080
Or what about Loras Tyrell, who’s the youngest
son in the books!

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:12.080
Let me know what you think!

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:15.400
So, those are my thoughts on the Lannisters
and Dorne in Season 6.

